From 94f1f06f99ebf83cd11650266b6f54a814906116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:49:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 03/50] Add liveness native module: engine, models, camera,
 bridge

New Android library module android/liveness
(io.mosip.registration.liveness.android), used by the app:
- libs/: the MOSIP liveness engine jars (liveness-api, -core, -analyzer,
  -fake 1.2.0.2) and src/main/assets/liveness/models/: the signed model
  bundle pad-2026.10.1, both copied byte for byte by Mosip26's
  android-integration/scripts/sync-engine.ps1 (engine-sync.txt records the
  engine commit and every file's SHA-256). CameraXFrameSource.java is Part
  1's camera source, synced from the same repository: edit it there.
  .gitattributes keeps the bundle and the jars byte-exact (no line-ending
  conversion), as in Mosip26: manifest.sig is checked over manifest.json.
- onnxruntime-android 1.31.0, CameraX 1.3.4 (core, camera2, lifecycle,
  view), androidx.core 1.12.0, clientmanager.
- AssetBundleSource: the bundle from the assets (capped reads); the engine
  verifies the signature. AndroidConfigProvider: synced global params, empty
  values as missing. AndroidAuditSink: engine audit records to the audit
  table (workflow -> REGISTRATION / LOGIN / REG_PACKET_LIST, HOME without a
  workflow; details as key=value;... cut to 2048 characters; written on a
  background thread; failures logged, never thrown).
- LivenessServiceHolder (Dagger singleton): the real engine (ONNX analyzer,
  assets bundle or a newer verified bundle in files/liveness-models) and the
  fake engine, a config override map, and preload() on a background thread
  at app start (time logged and audited; a failure is audited as
  MODEL_INTEGRITY_FAILED with its error code).
- TimedAnalyzerFactory: per-stage p50/p95 analysis times per session.
  LivenessMaps: event/result maps for Dart. BestFrameEncoder: JPEG q90.
- packagingOptions: the analyzer jar's copy of the models
  (liveness/models/**) is excluded from the APK in the module and the app;
  the engine jars' git.properties are merged.

Bridge (app):
- pigeon/liveness.dart, LivenessApi: isEnabled, policy, startSession
  (async; "" when disabled), retry, cancel, modelVersion, and
  setConfigOverride (debug builds only). One pigeon.sh line, Android only.
- Event channel io.mosip.registration_client/liveness/events: {kind:"event",
  ...} and {kind:"complete", ...}; the best frame only on PASSED, never
  logged. One session at a time (a new one cancels the old one and drops its
  callbacks); the Activity pausing cancels the session. A missing camera
  permission completes with FAILED / CAMERA_UNAVAILABLE.
- Platform view io.mosip.registration_client/liveness_preview: a PreviewView
  (FILL_CENTER, COMPATIBLE) that the next session binds its preview to.
- Dart: lib/platform_spi/liveness_service.dart (LivenessService,
  LivenessMessage) and lib/platform_android/liveness_service_impl.dart (asks
  for the camera permission, then starts the session).
- Wired through HostApiModule and MainActivity (setup, preload, onPause).

Tests: :liveness:testDebugUnitTest, 35 JVM tests (maps, config provider,
audit mapping and truncation, asset source, stage timing, YUV conversion).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
